  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Linear Programming: whole-number points in a region</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 1.4 (b) / Essential 1.4 (b): Give a whole-number point of a feasible region, and one that lies on a solid boundary of the region.</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 1, Section E, question 2 of Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP GCSE Mathematics: Higher 2 for AQA, Edexcel and OCR two-tier GCSE mathematics, Cambridge University Press, 2007: finding a whole-number point inside a region, made a construct-an-example question with a part on a solid boundary, with new regions.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
